# Frogger Game Project Audit

## Audit Scope

Static project audit of a React 19 + Vite + Tailwind + React Three Fiber browser game. Browser execution, Playwright, and visual browser tests were intentionally not used. Validation included source inspection and a production build check.

Verified command:

```bash
npm run build
```

Result: production build succeeds.

## Current Architecture

- Runtime stack: React, React DOM, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Three.js, React Three Fiber, lucide-react, Drei dependency present but not used in the inspected code.
- Main UI shell: `src/App.tsx`.
- Gameplay state and loop: `src/useGame.ts`.
- Pure gameplay core: `src/gameCore.ts`.
- Rendering and 3D procedural scene: `src/Scene.tsx`.
- Constants and procedural level generation: `src/gameConstants.ts`.
- Viewport fitting math: `src/viewMath.ts`.
- High score storage adapter: `src/highScoreStorage.ts`.
- Gameplay metrics adapter: `src/gameMetrics.ts`.
- Replay capture and QA playback: `src/gameReplay.ts`.
- Procedural Web Audio system: `src/audio.ts`.
- The project is a custom React/R3F game implementation, not a Phaser-based 2D game.
- Procedural generation now includes deterministic level modifiers, so some levels intentionally play differently rather than only becoming longer or faster.

## Implementation Progress

- Pure gameplay helpers were extracted into `src/gameCore.ts`.
- High score persistence now goes through `src/highScoreStorage.ts`.
- Transition helpers now cover goal, life-loss, and round-reset state changes.
- Developer collision diagnostics are available through the existing dev flag path.
- Dev mode now supports a `level` query flag for jumping to a target level at startup.
- Orthographic zoom fitting now lives in `src/viewMath.ts` instead of being hard-coded in the renderer.
- Gameplay event tracking now goes through `src/gameMetrics.ts` as a lightweight in-memory adapter.
- Gameplay events now flush into `src/gameMetricsStorage.ts` as a local persistence sink.
- Deterministic replay snapshots now go through `src/gameReplay.ts`, capturing seed, input sequence, and state summaries for QA reproduction.
- Generated levels now pass through a pure validation guard that checks structural fairness and modifier compatibility.
- Unit tests cover movement, collision, level structure, transition helpers, physical keyboard mapping, dev flags, storage, view math, metrics adapter behavior, metrics persistence, and replay snapshot encoding/decoding.
- Restart behavior now uses an explicit action instead of a synthetic keyboard event.
- Runtime frog and lane motion now live in refs, keeping React state on coarse UI and lifecycle boundaries.
- River landings now acquire a stable platform lock in the same simulation tick, so logs and turtles carry the frog without per-frame AABB reacquisition.
- Touch controls stay visible as the primary mobile input path, while keyboard help keeps its layout space but becomes fully transparent on phone-sized viewports.
- Keyboard controls now use physical `KeyboardEvent.code` mappings, so WASD, pause, restart, and dev-step controls do not depend on the active character layout.
- Audio cleanup now disconnects one-shot nodes after playback and detaches active music nodes on stop.
- Playable top bounds and river edge buffers now use named constants from `src/gameConstants.ts`.
- Several scene heights now use named render constants for water, board shell, frog shadow, and lane surfaces.
- Dev overlay can now show the frog's current row and column through a dedicated query flag.
- Score transition constants are now named in `src/gameCore.ts` instead of using raw literals.
- Lane classification helpers now centralize road, river, goal, and row lookup policy.
- The top HUD now uses the Figma-aligned compact capsule layout with `Geologica` typography, local UI assets, liquid-glass treatment, score, health or active bonus countdown, level, and pause.
- The pause overlay now matches the HMI Studio layout and exposes four visible master-volume segments plus a zero-volume state, synchronized mute behavior, resume control, and a functional Main Screen action guarded by the HMI Studio `98:995` confirmation dialog; Bonus Guide remains an intentional non-functional placeholder.
- The application now opens on the HMI Studio `96:575` start screen with responsive background, title, and frog parallax layers, matching language flags, shared mute state, and a short fade-through-black transition into gameplay.
- English and Russian copy is shared across the start screen, gameplay HUD and controls, pause, level-complete, game-over, and main-screen exit confirmation.
- Level-complete and game-over overlays now match their HMI Studio layouts, use the shared Geologica/liquid-glass UI language, remain adapters around the existing score, bonus, high-score, level-transition, and restart state, and render in the locale selected on the start screen.
- Camera framing now keeps the baseline orthographic zoom stable and follows the player with a lower-screen reserve for controls.
- Primary HUD indicators and controls now use local Figma-exported UI assets with lucide fallback icons for non-Figma bonus types instead of emoji glyphs or one-off inline SVG controls.
- The art direction sheet now lives in `project_context/Art Direction Sheet.md` as the stable visual reference.
- Decorative grass tufts now use instancing instead of spawning dozens of separate meshes per safe lane.
- Reduced-motion preferences now suppress screen shake and the main decorative bob/oscillation effects.
- Dev mode now includes a single-step simulation control for paused QA sessions.
- Step mode keeps the simulation paused across restart and level transition flows until an explicit step is requested.
- Collectible shield pickups now exist and grant a temporary protection state plus bonus score.
- Collectible slow-time pickups now exist and temporarily reduce hazard speed plus bonus score.
- Collectible current-anchor pickups now exist and temporarily suppress river drift plus bonus score.
- Collectible super-hop pickups now exist and temporarily extend hop range plus bonus score.
- Collectible fly pickups now exist and grant a short combo scoring window plus bonus score.
- Bonus pickups are mutually exclusive: collecting any bonus replaces the previous effect, clears its timer and runtime flags, and starts the new bonus with a full timer; the HUD displays one bonus icon.
- Perfect-clear bonus now exists for level clears with zero deaths and awards an extra score chunk.
- Time-challenge bonus now exists for fast level clears and is surfaced in the HUD timer.
- Challenge-session reward helpers now live in `src/gameChallenge.ts` instead of remaining embedded in `useGame.ts`.
- A lightweight in-memory metrics adapter records core gameplay events and flushes them into a separate local persistence sink.

